From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dariusz Majnert <dariusz.majnert@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 11:36:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] rs274ngc: add composable executor stdglue

Ported to v2.10.0-pre2. HalExecutor uses the Python hal module's
hal.Type and hal.Dir names (the HAL_BIT/HAL_S32/HAL_U32 spellings now
only exist as deprecated aliases). Its pins are bool, sint and uint,
which are 64 bits wide, so the opcode range is the 64-bit signed range
and request IDs wrap within 64 bits, still skipping zero. The
install-headless Makefile hunk is dropped: that target no longer exists
and a --disable-gui install already includes stdglue.py.

Generators are also closed when Interp::init() discards an active call
stack (EMC_TASK_PLAN_INIT), which does not go through unwind_call().
When the unwind starts inside the generator itself, for example M2 or a
failing call run through self.execute(), the generator cannot be closed
while it runs; the close is deferred until it yields or returns, and
pycall() then returns the unwind status (INTERP_EXIT or an error)
instead of continuing the unwound call.
